UIKit: run the video driver's entry points on the main thread.

Minecraft 26.3 (LWJGL 3.4.3) calls SDL from its own render thread, which then
becomes SDL's "main" (video) thread, while UIKit may only be used on the iOS
main thread. Each UIKit entry point in the device table hops to the main
thread with dispatch_sync, as VXGLFW.m does for earlier Minecraft versions.
GL entry points stay on the caller's thread (EAGLContext is per thread).
PumpEvents does nothing off the main thread: the app's own run loop delivers
touches, and SDL queues them thread-safely. Message boxes and pointer-lock
updates also go to the main thread.

